  "narrative": {
    "essence": "Three World Cup finals, zero trophies — the Netherlands carry the heaviest burden in world football. The greatest team never to win it. In 2026, with Van Dijk commanding the defense and a new generation of attackers bursting through, Oranje arrives with a genuine chance to finally end the curse.",
    "footballIdentity": "Total Football. Two words that encapsulate not just a tactical system but a philosophy, a worldview, a cultural identity. Johan Cruyff's Netherlands of 1974 didn't just play football differently — they changed what football was. Every Dutch player since has been measured against that standard, shaped by the Ajax academy system that has industrialized the production of technically excellent, positionally sophisticated footballers. The Dutch don't just play football, they theorize it.",
    "theMoment": "Van Dijk is 34 and at the summit of his powers, one of the best centre backs the game has seen. Frenkie de Jong, despite years of Barcelona turbulence, remains a midfielder of rare technical quality. And the next generation — Gakpo, Simons, Frimpong — are arriving. Koeman's challenge is to synthesize the old and new into something capable of not just reaching a final again, but winning one. The Dutch weight of footballing expectation is unique in world sport.",
    "momentType": "footballing"
  },
  "keyPlayers": [
    {
      "name": "Virgil van Dijk",
      "club": "Liverpool",
      "position": "Centre Back",
      "badge": "Captain",
      "note": "Arguably the best centre back of his generation — dominant in the air, commanding with the ball, and a leader whose presence transforms the teams he plays in. At 34, Van Dijk remains at the peak of his defensive powers at Liverpool, and as Netherlands captain he provides the stable foundation from which everything else is built."
    },
    {
      "name": "Frenkie de Jong",
      "club": "Barcelona",
      "position": "Central Midfielder",
      "badge": null,
      "note": "The natural heir to Dutch midfield royalty — de Jong's ability to receive the ball in tight spaces, turn under pressure, and play progressive passes into danger areas is elite. Despite turbulence at Barcelona, his quality is undimmed, and in a Netherlands shirt where the system is built for him, he operates at a level few midfielders in the world can match."
    },
    {
      "name": "Cody Gakpo",
      "club": "Liverpool",
      "position": "Left Wing / Striker",
      "badge": null,
      "note": "The most dangerous forward in the Dutch squad — Gakpo's combination of height, pace, and technical quality makes him a nightmare for any defender to contain. His ability to play centrally or wide gives Koeman tactical flexibility, and his Champions League experience with Liverpool means the biggest stages bring out his best football."
    },
    {
      "name": "Tijjani Reijnders",
