  "tactics": {
    "styleTags": [
      "Total Football Legacy",
      "Pressing",
      "Technical",
      "Offensive",
      "Possession"
    ],
    "tacticalNote": "Koeman's 4-3-3 draws heavily on Dutch tradition — Van Dijk and the center backs build from the back, feeding de Jong who then orchestrates the tempo. The wide forwards in Gakpo and the right winger press high and provide the width, while Reijnders operates as a mobile eight who arrives in dangerous positions late. The Netherlands want to dominate possession but are equally dangerous in transition, with the pace of their forwards threatening to run in behind.",
    "strength": "The defensive security of Van Dijk combined with the creative quality of de Jong and Simons gives Netherlands both solidity and attacking sophistication — a hard combination to match.",
    "vulnerability": "When the ball is won high and the Netherlands are caught in transition, the fullbacks' attacking positions leave space behind — Japan's pace could exploit this."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "De Jong's positioning between midfield lines — when he receives in tight spaces and turns, the Netherlands move from patient to dangerous in an instant",
    "Van Dijk's distribution from deep — his ability to play accurate long passes into wide areas is a key part of how the Netherlands bypass pressing teams",
    "Gakpo vs opposing right backs — his physicality and pace in wide areas create the overloads from which most Dutch attacks are launched"
